    "The confusion matrix shows that the model correctly classified a large number of low-rated movies (true negatives), while correctly identifying fewer high-rated movies (true positives). A noticeable number of high-rated movies were misclassified as low-rated (false negatives), indicating that the model tends to favor predicting the majority class.\n",
    "\n",
    "This pattern is also reflected in the classification metrics, where recall for the low-rated class is significantly higher than for the high-rated class. The class imbalance present in the dataset likely contributes to this behavior, causing the model to perform better at identifying low-rated movies while struggling to detect many high-rated movies."
