   "source": [
    "## 6.7 Logistic-Regression-Oberservations-With-Class-Weighting\n",
    "\n",
    "Because the dataset contains more low-rated movies than high-rated movies, the logistic regression model may become biased toward predicting the majority class. To address this issue, the model was retrained using class weighting.\n",
    "\n",
    "Using the parameter `class_weight='balanced', the logistic regression algorithm assigns higher importance to the minority class (high-rated movies) during training. This encourages the model to better identify high-rated movies.\n",
    "\n",
    "The balanced logistic regression model achieved an accuracy of approximately 71.1%, which is slightly lower than the original model. However, the recall for the high-rated class improved significantly from 0.35 to 0.72. This indicates that the balanced model is much better at identifying high-rated movies.\n",
    "\n",
    "Although overall accuracy decreased, the balanced model provides a more equitable classification across both classes and reduces the bias toward the majority class. This demonstrates how class imbalance can influence classification models and how class weighting can help improve detection of minority classes."
   ]
  },
